<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#entrepot">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Entrepôt</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as entrepot</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An entrepôt is a port or trading centre where goods are imported, stored and re-exported, often without further processing. Control of such hubs gave states wealth and influence; examples include <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adulis">Adulis</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeila">Zeila</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palembang">Palembang</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-malacca">Strait of Malacca</a> ports for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/entrepot.jpg" alt="Entrepôt" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jane023 · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entrepot_dok_Kadijksplein_Amsterdam.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
